  "synopsis": "Accepted for piece 03 as researcher guidance on making workflows inspectable: describe plans before collecting data, share code and variable definitions, and budget time for methodological review. Applying this advice to agent-assisted experiments is an editorial inference. This interview supplies practitioner perspectives, not measured autonomous-agent performance or independent corroboration of other studies. Its September 23 UTC publication falls within the run window; the report discussed was presented in June, and its September publication is only anticipated in the recording.",
  "limitations_and_counterevidence": "No controlled outcome evaluation, agent benchmark, held-out test, execution logs, hardware specification, quantified budget, or independent replication is supplied. The referenced report and survey are not supplied and cannot establish findings here. Efficiency and better-science assertions remain speaker claims. The first guest co-authored the report and describes providing training; the second is introduced as editor-in-chief of the Journal of Trial and Error. Preserve the first guest's explicit affirmation that authors remain necessary. Earlier encouragement that sharing is not time-consuming must be read alongside later advice to budget extra time; these remarks concern somewhat different scopes and do not establish a measured contradiction. Sharing materials does not require unrestricted sharing of sensitive data. Automatic transcription remains provisional: uncertain wording, names, and possible missing negations must not be repaired or used to establish speaker error. The selected segments are transcript evidence, not audio-verified quotations. These orientation fields cannot substitute for validated passage citations in later drafting.",
